<title>RUSSIA: Rouble eases after earlier fluctuations.</title>
<headline>Rouble eases after earlier fluctuations.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The rouble eased on Friday after an early rise caused by month-end payments and purchases of government securities, dealers said.</p>
<p> roubles/dollar	Nov 22 midday  Nov 22 early   Nov 21 close</p>
<p> today settlement    5,493-96	 5,489-91	 5,489-90</p>
<p> tomorrow settlement 5,497-99	 5,497-99	 5,494-96</p>
<p> overnight credit (%)   10-20	    20-35	    40-60</p>
<p>			   Nov 22				Nov 21</p>
<p> central bank	  5,489/99			    5,487/97</p>
<p> MICEX		   5,492				 5,489</p>
<p>&quot;Roubles were expensive in the morning, and banks started selling dollars for today settlement. But then somebody started offering roubles (for overnight credits), and the dollar firmed,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>Avtobank dealer Sergei Gornev said the rouble shortage was due to investments on the T-bill market and month-end payments by banks and their clients..</p>
<p>--Artyom Danielyan, Moscow newsroom (095) 941 8520</p>
